# the nudge: a layer's button held (ENV the chord, ARP the pings, LFO the bass, SEQ the drums) moves its sound a
# small step (a walk pulled back to the piece's recipe), says the biggest change and shows the layer's sound page;
# a tap is the page, as ever. Evolve nudges by itself, now and then on a phrase's first bar: at 100 it does, at 40
# (and under) never
listen
wait 2000
press ENV
wait 700
release ENV
wait 300
said CHORD NUDGE
expect view 8
press ARP
wait 700
release ARP
wait 300
said PINGS NUDGE
expect view 9
press LFO
wait 700
release LFO
wait 300
said BASS NUDGE
expect view 10
press SEQ
wait 700
release SEQ
wait 300
said DRUMS NUDGE
expect view 11
# a tap: the page (no nudge)
tap ENV
wait 300
expect view 1
said_none NUDGE
# Evolve 40 (Basic's): two minutes playing, nothing nudged (saved, then still saved)
tap HOME
wait 300
expect view 0
tap SAVE
wait 300
expect dirty 0
wait 120000
expect dirty 0
# Evolve 100: two minutes, the sound nudged (the project changed)
spin K2 60
wait 200
expect par5 100
tap SAVE
wait 300
expect dirty 0
wait 120000
expect dirty 1
